t of Appeals\">121 L. Ed. 2d 305</a></span> (1992) (per curiam). Justice Stevens dissents. See <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9432691\"><a href=\"/opinion/112790/martin-v-district-of-columbia-court-of-appeals/#4\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Martin v. District of Columbia Court of Appeals\">id., at 4</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9432691\"><a href=\"/opinion/112790/martin-v-district-of-columbia-court-of-appeals/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Martin v. District of Columbia Court of Appeals\">113 S. Ct. 397</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9432691\"><a href=\"/opinion/112790/martin-v-district-of-columbia-court-of-appeals/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Martin v. District of Columbia Court of Appeals\">121 L. Ed. 2d 305</a></span>, and cases cited therein.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}